Nothing special about this ascension except for the very final throw
of the dice.  After offering the Amulet on Astral I set about making a
YAAP by marking & copying the text from the dos window (Windows XP). 
I accidentally clicked on "close" instead of "mark" at one point, and
the window closed.  I was a little annoyed about not gettting all the
inventory & conduct info, but not too grumpy.  I checked in the
Nethack directory and discovered that the savefile was still intact. 
I fired up Nethack again and loaded Akinomoto, and discovered that he
was standing on the altar on Astral with no Amulet.  I therefore had
to #quit in order to get the dump and the high score table entry.  Is
this a bug?  Anyway, story & edited dump below.

[Story]

Went to Soko first.  On the level with the entrance to Soko sat on a
throne and genocided mind flayers.  Soko had the amulet.

Minetown was a bones file.  Random X (a monk by the looks of it) had
apparently picked a fight with the priest and come off worst.  The
altar room was chaos and there were insects running everywhere. 
Random X's grave was on the altar, and included a very, very heavy bag
and a gray stone!  There was a peaceful priest wandering around.  I
converted the altar, managed to pick up the bag to uncurse it and then
sorted out all the stuff.  Spent some time saccing and got
snickersnee.  Got a full inventory ID and the gray stone turned out to
be a luckstone, so didn't bother going down to mine's end.  Did a
little alchemy to take hp to 211.

Continued down the dungeon.  On dlvl 11 found an aligned priest in a
temple.  Decided to move my stash there from minetown.  Got attacked
by soldiers, one of which hit me with a cockatrice corpse.  First time
this has ever happened to me - lucky I had a lizard corpse!  One of
the soldiers dropped a +5 pair of yugake to make up for it though -
took my AC down to -19.

On the way down to Medusa's fell through a trap door.  Went up the
stairs and came face to face with the lady herself.  Killed her fairly
easily but then realised that I had no means of crossing the water. 
Went down to the castle and realised I had no musical instrument and
no wand of striking.

Went on a killfest on dlvl 25 to try and find a musical instrument,
means of crossing water or a wand of striking.  An encounter with a
master lich increased my AC from -19 to -4 when he destroyed some of
my better pieces of armour.  Eventually found a wand of striking when
a grey elf dropped one.

Went down to the castle, slipped on a ring of conflict and then zapped
the drawbridge with the wand of striking.  An air elemental came
across, swallowed me and then dropped me into the water blanking all
my potions and scrolls.  Got the wand and wished (1) for 2 blessed
scrolls of charging.  Then had to recharge.  Wished (2) up a ring of
levitation so that I could get to the dragons.  None of them dropped
scales.  Decided to head back to the stash and sort through all the
gear.

Wished (3) for a magic marker.  Reverse geno'd gray dragons and got
some scales.  Made armour.

Went down to Gehennom.  Paid off Asmodeus.  Got brain sucked by a MMF.
 Went back up to stash, ID'd everything and then wished (4) for a
magic marker.  Wrote charging, which I'd forgotten - second time
lucky.  Charged up my 2 used up magic markers, wrote enchant armour
scrolls with all three of the markers.  Used last with on a helm of
telepathy, and got AC down to -34.  Also did some alchemy to get hp to
around 350 ish.  Went back to Gehennom to continue down.  Finally got
shock resistance from a storm giant corpse.

Did Gehennom, went back and mapped dungeon after the mindflayers and
sorted out all the gear for the ascension run.  Killed Wizard and High
Priest.  Had a nasty experience on level 36 - Wizard stole the amulet
and then stole the Tsurugi of Muramasa straight afterwards.  This left
me with no weapon to kill him with.  Followed him but then an arch
lich turned up.  Eventually had to engrave Elbereth.  Killed
everything I could, but couldn't kill the lich.  The Wizard went
upstairs.  Eventually made a dash for the stairs, sat on them and beat
the lich to death with a rusty +0 pick-axe.  Killed everything else on
the level, then went up after the Wizard with a wand of death I'd
found.  Killed him and he didn't have the amulet - which meant it must
be downstairs and he must have been killed by a black dragon or a wand
of death.  Eventually found the amulet, the Tsurugi, the Bell and the
Book - right on the upstairs where I'd been standing during the battle
with the arch lich!

A similar problem happened on level 9 - this time used the magic lamp
to try and get scrolls of charging to re-charge the wands of death,
but the lamp didn't work.  Burned elbereth again.  Got down to 30 hp
out of 499 and prayed to get back up to 499.  Eventually a cockatrice
was summoned by one of the arch liches and I turned everyone into
statues.

Got revenge by slicing the Wizard in half on the Plane of Earth.  On
the plane of earth noticed that the lamp was still called magic.  I
rubbed it again and got a wish.  Thought for a long time and then went
for a magic marker.  Then realised I had no scrolls...

Died on plane of fire being stuck in lava.  Displeased god by praying.
 Whipped on an amulet of life saving.  Eventually realised that I
could just walk out of the lava, but by this point I'd already died
once.

The plane of water took a long time.

On the Astral Plane, went for the middle as that was Pestillence (I
have a grudge).  Killed him with a wand of death and got to the altar
very quickly - in about 50 moves.  Turned out to be the right altar. 
Offered the Amulet and then set about making the YAAP.  Below is the
screenshot, but the info is all from the dump after I #quit.

